# requirements/pr-and-gates.feature
# Factory stages 12–14 — open the PR against the target branch, then wait for
# every PR-triggered workflow to go green, fixing failures in a bounded loop.

Feature: Pull request and gate loop
  As the factory
  I want a pull request against the target branch once the review is clean
  so that the finished work enters the target repo only through the human gate

  Background:
    Given the test-and-review loop ended with zero problems
    And the AI branch is named ai/<issue_number>

  @pr
  Scenario: A pull request is opened against the target branch
    Given GH_TOKEN has pull-requests:write on the target repo
    When the pr-open stage runs
    Then a PR is opened from the AI branch to the configured TARGET_BRANCH
    And the PR body is generated by pi from the requirements, plans and review

  @pr
  Scenario: The PR body links back to the work
    When the pr-open stage runs
    Then the PR body references the source issue
    And the PR body serves as the final status report

  @gates
  Scenario: All PR-triggered workflows must be green
    Given the PR is open
    When the pr-gates stage waits for every pull_request workflow on the PR
    Then the stage succeeds only when all of them are green

  @gates
  Scenario: A failed gate is fixed and re-checked
    Given one PR-triggered workflow is red
    When the pr-gate-fix stage fixes the failure and re-runs pr-gates
    Then the loop repeats until all gates are green

  @gates @safety
  Scenario: The gate loop is bounded
    Given the gate loop reached MAX_LOOPS without going green
    When the loop would start another iteration
    Then the pipeline stops and reports the failing gate

  @pr @safety
  Scenario: Merging stays a human decision
    Given the PR is open and all gates are green
    Then the factory does not merge the PR itself
    And merging is manual unless auto-merge is explicitly opted in
